1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,077
Football is more than the scoreline.

2
00:00:03,117 --> 00:00:09,508
PULSE XI turns synthetic match events into intelligence you can inspect, compare and replay.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,171
A synthetic match replays from recorded events.

4
00:00:14,211 --> 00:00:19,603
Every statistic is computed from them, and the screen stays steady.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,924
Pick a goal and ask why it matters.

6
00:00:24,964 --> 00:00:29,895
The drawer shows the calculation and its source events.

7
00:00:29,935 --> 00:00:34,776
One moment, three stories, all citing the same events.

8
00:00:34,816 --> 00:00:40,651
The director's cue stays a proposal until a producer approves it.

9
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:48,084
Change the audience or the language, and the wording changes.

10
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:55,224
The facts do not.

11
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,939
Control vs Chaos shows how the rhythm of play shifted.

12
00:00:59,979 --> 00:01:04,248
The pass inspector rates each pass with an explainable heuristic.

13
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:11,701
Control Room: a deterministic engine runs the match.

14
00:01:11,741 --> 00:01:18,462
Save a checkpoint, change a tactic, run a paired comparison against the baseline.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,779
Then verify the result independently.

16
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,275
Highlights are built only from event data.

17
00:01:29,315 --> 00:01:34,203
Each clip shows its score and its source events, with no match footage.

18
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,801
Synthetic and rule-based.

19
00:01:40,841 --> 00:01:45,489
Microsoft Agent Framework path verified offline.

20
00:01:45,529 --> 00:01:47,638
Code public on GitHub.
